  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1050 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nA 600 dam upper ridge is centered over the Mid-South tonight.\nThis feature will dominate the region's weather through this\nweekend while slowly retrograding westward. Near record to record\nhighs are expected each day with temperatures reaching into the\nupper 90s to low 100s degrees. Triple-digit afternoon heat index\nvalues will be common, and the Heat Advisory is in effect through\n8 pm Saturday. Don't let your guard down on the heat. Check the\nback seat, stay in the AC, and stay hydrated.\n\nA mid-level trough will move into the Middle Mississippi Valley\nand Southern Plains on Monday with a weak cold front moving into\nthe region. Meanwhile, an upper low in the NE Gulf will result in\nincreasing moisture over the Southeast U.S. As a result of these\ntwo features, rain chances will increase early next week.\nHowever, QPF amounts look fairly paltry for now, at less than a\nhalf inch through next Wednesday.\n\nStarting to see some divergence in the models by the middle to\nend of next week, with a large spread in NBM temperature\nguidance. Some guidance is showing more troughing over the\neastern CONUS and possibly cooler temps for the Mid-South.\nHowever, the majority of the guidance still favors at least some\nupper ridging continuing across the Mid-South along with above\nnormal temperatures well into next week.",
